  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (`7 witnesses, 12 names, composes NRS_484B_253_o1`), so 5 of the 6 gate runs are unused.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_253_o2.lean`):\n- **Applicability:** the subject is on a carrier c2 that enters intersection X and is not yet in X. Another vehicle t is in X, has declared `int.left_turn` at X, and entered X from a carrier c1 that also enters X and runs opposite to c2 (dot product below −`p.oncoming_heading_cos`).\n- **The signal:** t showed a left signal, by indicator or by arm, at some point since it last came onto c1.\n- **The turn:** t has been moving in X since its current movement began. At that start it complied with `NRS_484B_253_o1`, written as `.rule` with `subject ↦ t`; this is \"having so yielded\".\n- **Obligation:** the full selection is restated over every X, c2 and t. The subject must not touch t, and must not keep moving while its closest approach to t falls within `p.conflict_horizon` at a centre distance below `p.conflict_centre_clearance`.\n- I declared no narrowings; the formulas follow the node's wording directly.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_253_o2.lean`): all six planned scenarios are built from one map: X, plus a northbound lane c1 and a southbound lane c2 that both enter it. I added a seventh, `branch_3` (violated), where t signals only by arm, so the hand-signal option is tested on its own.\n\n**Caveat:** I couldn't read o1's file, so `branch_1` relies on o1 judging t as not having yielded when its turn began. In that scene the subject is 20 m off with a closest approach 1.6 s ahead at 2 m. The gate accepted it, so o1 does decide it that way.\n\nOne shell command (`wc` on Core files) was blocked because only the gate command is allowed. I used the Read tool instead, and nothing was lost.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
